Mapping
Id	Rule	Status	Derived from	Module
M1	the input is an OTLP JSON Lines file; TracesData and LogsData carry the eight, MetricsData none	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP file; Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes	integrations/otlp_json
M2	lines are read in the file's order; nothing is sorted	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP file	integrations/otlp_json
M3	fields with unknown names are ignored	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP JSON	integrations/otlp_json
M4	ids are written as their hex text and compared without regard to case	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP JSON	integrations/otlp_json
M5	the eight are found by their attribute keys, structured or as a JSON string	derived	Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes; the eight GenAI set artefacts	integrations/otlp_json
M6	each of the eight has sheets of its own; input and output messages are kept apart	derived	the eight GenAI set artefacts	_system_instructions; _tool_definitions; _input_messages; _output_messages; _tool_call_arguments; _tool_call_result; _memory_records; _retrieval_documents; _parts
M7	a schema definition with fields of its own is a sheet of its own	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (same domains); Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes (fields)	_system_instructions; _tool_definitions; _input_messages; _output_messages; _tool_call_arguments; _tool_call_result; _memory_records; _retrieval_documents; _parts
M8	a nonsimple field is a child sheet; each row's pointer extends its parent's pointer, so it carries its parent's key	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (nonsimple domain; normalization); Content › Integrations › JSON Pointer	_relations
M9	every row is keyed by traceId, spanId and pointer: its span, and its place in the attribute value from the value's root	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP records; Content › Integrations › JSON Pointer; Content › Integrations › relations (normalization)	_relations
M10	a value of any shape is one sheet, a row per node: pointer, type and value	derived	Content › Integrations › JSON Pointer; Content › Integrations › JSON (value kinds)	_relations
M11	order is kept by the pointer's zero-based indexes	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (rows unordered); Content › Integrations › JSON (arrays ordered); Content › Integrations › JSON Pointer (zero-based index); Content › Integrations › GenAI input messages (order)	_relations
M12	an enum is a simple value, so a column	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (simple domain)	_system_instructions; _tool_definitions; _input_messages; _output_messages; _tool_call_arguments; _tool_call_result; _memory_records; _retrieval_documents; _parts
M13	properties beyond a schema go to their object's value sheet	derived	Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes (further properties); M10	_relations
M14	numbers are written as the source writes them	derived	Content › Integrations › JSON (range and precision may be limited)	_relations
M15	values MTSV cannot represent are not written	derived	Content › Format › fields and sheet names	_relations
M16	names are the sources' own: traceId and spanId from OTLP JSON, pointer from JSON Pointer, type and value from JSON, the fields from the schemas	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP JSON (keys); Content › Integrations › JSON Pointer; Content › Integrations › JSON (value kinds); Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes (fields)	_relations; _system_instructions; _tool_definitions; _input_messages; _output_messages; _tool_call_arguments; _tool_call_result; _memory_records; _retrieval_documents; _parts
M17	a log record without trace and span ids is keyed by its position in the file	open	Content › Integrations › OTLP records (ids optional); no source keys it	_relations
M18	the output is one MTSV file: every sheet of the Sheets order, each with its header, and no records where the input has none	derived	Content › Format › sheets	_relations
M19	null, the empty string and an absent field in a schema sheet	open	Content › Format › fields (a field is text); no source tells the three apart in text	_system_instructions; _tool_definitions; _input_messages; _output_messages; _tool_call_arguments; _tool_call_result; _memory_records; _retrieval_documents; _parts
